<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Fire of Hamburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1842</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Fire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> broke out on 5 May 1842 and burned for four days, destroying about a quarter of the old town, including the town hall and several churches. About fifty people died and some 20,000 were left homeless. The rebuilding, planned in part by the English engineer William Lindley, gave Hamburg a modern sewer system and a new centre around the Inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alster">Alster</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-fire-of-hamburg.jpg" alt="Great Fire of Hamburg" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Suhr (1788-) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pincerno_-_Suhr_-_Der_Gro%C3%9Fe_Brand_1842.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
